KZ3 patch 2150 (ENHANCEMENT, experimental, diagnostics): opt-in XeSS jitter experiments and draw coverage.

Built on patch 2149. With none of the switches set the Halton rendering of 2149 is unchanged. The switches scale the
projection and the execute jitter independently (KZ3_XESS_PROJECTION_SCALE_X/Y, KZ3_XESS_EXECUTE_SCALE_X/Y, -2..2,
default 1), choose an alternating two-phase sample (KZ3_XESS_JITTER_PATTERN=two-phase, default halton), lag the execute
jitter by one contiguous valid frame (KZ3_XESS_EXECUTE_JITTER_LAG=1, default 0), and log the pre-submission draw
eligibility every N frames (KZ3_XESS_JITTER_TRACE=N, default 0 = off). Lag resets across holds, failures and context
changes. They exist to isolate the remaining whole-scene jitter (docs/XESS.md, "Known problems"). Parsing and counters
are in port/kz3/xess_diagnostics.h, host-tested by tools/smoke/test_xess_diagnostics.c/.sh.

